WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:14.574
Sara stared at Mr. Carrisford, startled.

2
00:00:14.575 --> 00:00:19.364
His expression had changed. Was something wrong?

3
00:00:19.365 --> 00:00:23.114
"You were born in India?" he exclaimed.

4
00:00:23.115 --> 00:00:30.025
"Come here." Mr. Carrisford held out his hand to Sara.

5
00:00:30.026 --> 00:00:35.895
She went to him and laid her hand in his. "Yes, I was."

6
00:00:35.896 --> 00:00:42.581
"And you live next door?" he went on. "But you're not one of the students?"

7
00:00:42.582 --> 00:00:49.264
"I used to be a student, but now . . ." A sad smile crossed Sara's face.

8
00:00:49.265 --> 00:00:54.579
"Now I don't know who I am. I sleep in the attic with the kitchen maid.

9
00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:58.188
I run errands for the cook, and do whatever she tells me.

10
00:00:58.189 --> 00:01:02.887
And I teach the little ones their lessons."

11
00:01:02.888 --> 00:01:11.170
"Question her, Mr. Carmichael." The sick gentleman sank back in his chair. "I'm too weak."

12
00:01:11.171 --> 00:01:15.425
The big, kind father of the Large family had daughters.

13
00:01:15.426 --> 00:01:19.159
He knew just how to talk to girls Sara's age.

14
00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:24.047
"You used to be a student?" Mr. Carmichael asked kindly.

15
00:01:24.048 --> 00:01:29.175
"Yes, when my papa first took me to the school," Sara replied.

16
00:01:29.176 --> 00:01:33.206
"Where is he now?" Mr. Carmichael asked.

17
00:01:33.207 --> 00:01:37.613
"He died in India," Sara said very quietly.

18
00:01:37.614 --> 00:01:43.396
"He lost all his money and there was no one left to care for me, or pay Miss Minchin."

19
00:01:43.397 --> 00:01:48.799
"Carmichael!" called out Mr. Carrisford. "Carmichael!"

20
00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:53.542
"We must not frighten her," Mr. Carmichael said quietly.

21
00:01:53.543 --> 00:01:55.932
Then he turned back to Sara.

22
00:01:55.933 --> 00:02:00.671
"So you were sent up into the attic and turned into a servant. Is that right?"

23
00:02:00.672 --> 00:02:07.394
"Yes," Sara said. "There was no money, and I belong to nobody."

24
00:02:07.395 --> 00:02:11.738
"How did your father lose his money?" Mr. Carrisford asked.

25
00:02:11.739 --> 00:02:18.325
He took a few deep breaths to stay calm.

26
00:02:18.326 --> 00:02:26.104
"He did not lose it himself." Sara explained how her father had invested in his friend's diamond mines.

27
00:02:26.105 --> 00:02:31.480
"He was very fond of this friend, but he trusted him too much."

28
00:02:31.481 --> 00:02:36.728
The sick gentleman gasped. "What was your father's name?"

29
00:02:36.729 --> 00:02:40.052
"Captain Ralph Crewe."

30
00:02:40.053 --> 00:02:44.260
"It's the child!" cried Mr. Carrisford.

31
00:02:44.261 --> 00:02:48.650
"What is he talking about?" Sara asked Mr. Carmichael.

32
00:02:48.651 --> 00:02:51.906
"Mr. Carrisford was your father's friend.

33
00:02:51.907 --> 00:02:56.366
He didn't really lose your father's money. He only thought he did.

34
00:02:56.367 --> 00:03:00.596
He was terribly upset, and that made him very ill."

35
00:03:00.597 --> 00:03:04.284
"Oh, how awful!" said Sara.

36
00:03:04.285 --> 00:03:09.696
"You are now a very wealthy young lady," continued Mr. Carmichael.

37
00:03:09.697 --> 00:03:13.560
"We've been searching for you for a long time."

38
00:03:13.561 --> 00:03:18.515
"And I was right next door!" Sara said in amazement.

39
00:03:18.516 --> 00:03:22.928
"I often saw you pass by my house," Mr. Carrisford said.

40
00:03:22.929 --> 00:03:25.431
"You always looked so miserable.

41
00:03:25.432 --> 00:03:29.750
I couldn't find my friend's daughter, but I could help you."

42
00:03:29.751 --> 00:03:35.983
Sara was very surprised. "You sent the beautiful things to me?"

43
00:03:35.984 --> 00:03:40.340
"Yes, with the help of Ram Dass."

44
00:03:40.341 --> 00:03:46.547
"Then you're my mysterious friend!" Sara gave Mr. Carrisford a big hug.

45
00:03:46.548 --> 00:03:49.779
"Oh, thank you!"

46
00:03:49.780 --> 00:03:55.779
"You don't have to go back to the school," he said. "Would you like that?"

47
00:03:55.780 --> 00:04:00.562
"Oh yes, but Miss Minchin will be upset."

48
00:04:00.563 --> 00:04:04.594
Meanwhile the headmistress had learned that Sara was next door.

49
00:04:04.595 --> 00:04:07.076
She was very angry.

50
00:04:07.077 --> 00:04:13.686
She marched over to Mr. Carrisford's house, and Ram Dass led her into the sitting room.

51
00:04:13.687 --> 00:04:18.358
"Go home at once!" Miss Minchin ordered Sara.

52
00:04:18.359 --> 00:04:22.053
"I'm sure you're disturbing everyone!"

53
00:04:22.054 --> 00:04:27.352
"No," said Mr. Carrisford. He patted Sara's hand.

54
00:04:27.353 --> 00:04:31.022
"Sara will be living here from now on."

55
00:04:31.023 --> 00:04:34.899
"Here?" Miss Minchin exclaimed.

56
00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:38.683
"Perhaps I should explain," Mr. Carmichael said.

57
00:04:38.684 --> 00:04:41.944
He told her the story of the diamond mines.

58
00:04:41.945 --> 00:04:46.998
"We've been looking for Sara. She's the heiress to a huge fortune."

59
00:04:46.999 --> 00:04:50.382
Miss Minchin was stunned at this news.

60
00:04:50.383 --> 00:04:55.148
But she wasn't going to let Sara get away now that she was rich.

61
00:04:55.149 --> 00:05:00.546
"Captain Crewe left Sara in my charge," the headmistress insisted.

62
00:05:00.547 --> 00:05:06.458
"She must return to my school until she's an adult. It's the law."

63
00:05:06.459 --> 00:05:10.318
"No, it's not the law," said Mr. Carmichael.

64
00:05:10.319 --> 00:05:14.001
He knew about such things because he was a lawyer.

65
00:05:14.002 --> 00:05:19.173
"I'm sure Sara wants to return home with me," Miss Minchin said.

66
00:05:19.174 --> 00:05:22.336
"You know I've always been fond of you, Sara.

67
00:05:22.337 --> 00:05:26.465
If it hadn't been for me, you would have starved!"

68
00:05:26.466 --> 00:05:31.755
Mr. Carrisford lost his temper. "She was starving in your attic!"

69
00:05:31.756 --> 00:05:38.007
"You're not fond of me," Sara chimed in, looking at the headmistress.

70
00:05:38.008 --> 00:05:42.880
"The school is not my home, and you've treated me cruelly.

71
00:05:42.881 --> 00:05:45.489
I won't go back with you."

72
00:05:45.490 --> 00:05:51.298
"Fine," snapped Miss Minchin, "but you'll never see your friends again.

73
00:05:51.299 --> 00:05:53.704
I'll make sure that Lottie and Ermengarde—"

74
00:05:53.705 --> 00:05:57.133
"Don't be ridiculous," said Mr. Carmichael.

75
00:05:57.134 --> 00:06:01.896
"Their parents won't let them refuse Sara's invitations to visit here."

76
00:06:01.897 --> 00:06:05.042
Miss Minchin turned to leave.

77
00:06:05.043 --> 00:06:09.531
"You'll soon find out what Sara is like," she said to the men.

78
00:06:09.532 --> 00:06:14.694
"She's dishonest and spoiled." She spun toward Sara.

79
00:06:14.695 --> 00:06:18.957
"I suppose you think that you're a princess again!"

80
00:06:18.958 --> 00:06:28.661
With that, Miss Minchin returned to the school and started yelling at Miss Amelia.
